{ Train as White. Replay the opening from the initial position. }
1. e3 { White opens the bishop’s diagonal. } c5 2. Ba6 { White offers the bishop on a6. } Nxa6 { This is the Polish Defense position. } *

[Event "Defeating the Polish Defense"]
[StudyName "Defeating the Polish Defense"]
[ChapterName "Draw the c-pawn to b4"]
[Variant "Antichess"]
[Result "*"]

{ Train as White. Replay the opening from the initial position. }
1. e3 { White opens the bishop’s diagonal. } c5 2. Ba6 { White offers the bishop on a6. } Nxa6 { This is the Polish Defense position. } 3. b4 { Advance the b-pawn to draw Black’s c-pawn away from c5. } cxb4 { Black captures with the c-pawn. White now has the position we want. } *

[Event "Defeating the Polish Defense"]
[StudyName "Defeating the Polish Defense"]
[ChapterName "The key move: 4. d3"]
[Variant "Antichess"]
[Result "*"]

{ Train as White. Replay the opening from the initial position. }
1. e3 { White opens the bishop’s diagonal. } c5 2. Ba6 { White offers the bishop on a6. } Nxa6 { This is the Polish Defense position. } 3. b4 { Advance the b-pawn to draw Black’s c-pawn away from c5. } cxb4 { Black captures with the c-pawn. White now has the position we want. } 4. d3 { The key move in this repertoire is d3. This is the starting point for the deeper branches we will add. } *
